src/shim/tests/i86corpus/ -- .CMD files src/shim/tests/i86test.c reads.  Test input, nothing else.

PIP.CMD, ED.CMD, GENCMD.CMD, SUBMIT.CMD, ASM86.CMD, STAT.CMD, HELP.CMD,
TOD.CMD and HELP's data file HELP.HLP are Digital Research's own CP/M-86 1.1
(IBM PC) files, unmodified, from the cpm86pc drop of the Unofficial CP/M Web
Site.  Licensed by the 9 July 2022 grant from Bryan Sparks (President, DRDOS,
Inc.) at <http://cpm.z80.de/license.html>, which carries no distribution
restriction.

They are 8086 code, run by the CP/M-86 shim on the host and, through
tests/verify.mk, on the machine.  Our own utilities are native Z8000 programs
-- src/cmd/pip.c and src/cmd/stat.c are DRI's sources rebuilt as .Z8K -- so
these are here as known-answer tests for the shim, not as the system's tools.

DDT86.CMD is DRI's CP/M-86 debugger (version 1.2), unmodified, from the same
drop under the same grant.  It is the one real caller of BDOS functions 57
and 59, and it drives INT 3, the trap flag and the vector table.
